<title>FRANCE: Lowest French wheat bid covers 115,000 T exports.</title>
<headline>Lowest French wheat bid covers 115,000 T exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The lowest rebate offer submitted through France at Thursday's EU grain auction covers the export of 115,000 tonnes of soft wheat, grain trade sources said.</p>
<p>EU grain firms bid in France to export a total of 1.32 million tonnes of soft wheat at rebates ranging from 16.47 to 21.74 Ecus per tonne, France's grain office reported.  </p>
<p>Traders provided the following cumulative breakdown of soft wheat and barley bids submitted through France. (Refunds in Ecus per tonne).</p>
<p>SOFT WHEAT</p>
<p>    Tonnage			  Maximum refund</p>
<p>    115,000			  16.47</p>
<p>    145,000			  17.00</p>
<p>    345,000			  17.50</p>
<p>    360,000			  17.75</p>
<p>    593,000			  18.00</p>
<p>    878,000			  18.50</p>
<p>  1,322,200			  21.74</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>   Tonnage			   Maximum refund</p>
<p>     25,000			  30.49</p>
<p>     50,000			  31.00</p>
<p>    125,000			  32.00</p>
<p>    143,600			  34.26</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
